                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Hellpoint is basically Dark Souls but set in far future on a space station orbiting a black hole. It mixes sci-fi setting mixed with magic and everything has a survival-horror undertone. The station on which the game is set is like a maze filled with loot to find, bosses to fight, abilities to unlock and cryptic NPC to interact with.\n\nMy first impressions were mixed because how there seemed to be overall lack of direction, then I defeated the first boss and the game became much more enjoyable (immediately after it you unlock main hub, get first set of armour, access to crafting stations etc).\n\nThe game can be quite frustrating and confusing at first due to how poorly UI and some gameplay elements are explained but once you get past that it is a quite good souls-like.",
